- Story & Context: The closer begins at the highest tape saturation level on the EP. Voices arrive thick and slightly compressed, harmonium reeds push against the machine, and Nadeem's low guitar chords blur at the edges. The arrangement then moves backward. Every eight bars Mara reduces tape drive; Hamza removes one clap layer; Samina closes one harmonium register; Nadeem lengthens the silence between chords. The vocal call-and-response remains constant while everything around it becomes cleaner and smaller. In the final section, the tape path is bypassed entirely. Areeba sings one last phrase dry in the room. The response group answers without instruments, and the courtyard ambience continues for several seconds after the final consonant.
